  "messages": "maria: Heads up \u2014 noticed a few KB pages where embedded widgets (Figma/Miro iframes) aren't showing and there's no accessible fallback/alt. Example: /kb/runtime/troubleshooting shows a broken thumbnail + 404 when iframe load fails :frowning:  https://staging.kb/internal/example-snap.png\nryan: I can take a quick sweep today. do we have a curated list or a query I can run? :calendar:\nsophia: Usually the issue is missing `title` on the iframe and no <noscript> image fallback. For static images we just need proper markdown alt text.\nnash: here's a tiny snippet that covers both iframe fallback and static preview \u2014 paste into the MDX where the embed lives:\n```html\n<iframe src=\"https://www.figma.com/embed?embed_host=redwood&...\" title=\"Network diagram: request routing\" loading=\"lazy\"></iframe>\n<noscript>\n  <img src=\"/assets/previews/network-diagram.png\" alt=\"Preview: network diagram showing request routing and cache layers\" />\n</noscript>\n```\nash: for plain markdown images, do `![short alt text](/path/to/img.png)` \u2014 keep alt concise but useful.\ndocs-bot: scan-complete \u2014 9 files flagged by embed-alt-checker: /kb/runtime/troubleshooting, /kb/infra/cache, /kb/onboarding/architecture, plus 6 more. See report: https://internal.tools/docs-scans/6868686868\nmaria: perfect, thanks. ryan can you open PR(s) and tag @docs-team for review? please add a short changelog entry so we can track accessibility fixes. :thumbsup:\nryan: will do. opening a single PR with multiple small commits to keep history tidy. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3821 \u2014 assigning reviewers @sophia @ash. ETA EOD PST.\nsophia: quick QA note \u2014 link-checker still passes since 200 is returned, but axe/accessibility flagged missing alt. adding a follow-up rule to the CI so this fails loudly next week.\nmaria: thanks everyone. leaving a short note in the runbook (kb-runbook/embed-fallbacks) describing the pattern and how to test locally. ping me if anything unexpected pops up. :hand:",
